timestamp=2026-11-09T11:51:57.394Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Find which file farms are missing calibration\ncal_set = set(['FARM_A', 'FARM_B', 'FARM_C', 'FARM_D', 'FARM_E', 'FARM_F', 'FARM_G', 'FARM_H', 'FARM_I', 'FARM_J', 'FARM_K', 'FARM_L', 'FARM_M', 'FARM_N', 'FARM_O', 'FARM_P', 'FARM_Q', 'FARM_R', 'FARM_S', 'FARM_T', 'FARM_U', 'FARM_V', 'FARM_W', 'FARM_X'])\n# but cal has exactly these 24. Files have more: AA-AH (8 more) and Y,Z (2 more)? Also A is common. So files have AA- AH (8) + Y,Z (2) = 10 extra farms with no calibration? Also B-X (23 farms) plus A gives 24 farms that DO have calibration. Y,Z are in files but not in calibration - 2 more. AA-AH are 8 more. So total 24 + 10 = 34. Yes.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
