timestamp=2026-11-09T11:52:14.299Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Maybe these extra farm_ids are the ones without calibration - but the task says 24 farms total.\n# The task states: \"An operator manages a fleet of 24 solar photovoltaic farms. Compute the total real energy production in kilowatt-hours (kWh) on the UTC reporting day 2024-03-15 (the half-open window [2024-03-15 00:00:00 UTC, 2024-03-16 00:00:00 UTC)) for each farm.\"\n# Also: \"Return a dict keyed by `farm_id` with one entry per farm. Use 0 if a farm has no valid readings.\"\n# And calibration is given for farms - looks like the 24 farms are those in calibration JSON (24 entries). So the extra production files (Y,Z,AA-AH) might be for farms that are not in the \"24 solar photovoltaic farms\" fleet? Or they might be part of it but missing calibration data? That needs to be interpreted.\n# Let us look up these extra farms in registry via other means - maybe farm_name pattern? Or look at production data to infer.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
