timestamp=2026-11-09T11:59:09.962Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So one of the duplicates has NaN or is the \"other\" value. Also for FARM_H, calibration says value column is 'yield ' (with space?) and offset is -500. So the first 'yield' column has values matching offset pattern? -500.0 - that suggests it's the raw value before/related to calibration? But the actual measured value we need is the one to which calibration_offset is applied per the domain rule: \"The calibration_offset is defined as: (recorded value) - (true value).\"\n# But we also have the value_column_name specified. Let us look up each farm's value column name from calibration.\nimport json\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/sensors_calibration.json') as f:\n    cal = json.load(f)\nfarms = cal['enterprise_platform']['deployment_environments']['system_config']['farms']\nfor fid in ['FARM_N', 'FARM_H']:\n    print(fid, farms[fid]['calibration_data'])\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
