timestamp=2026-11-09T12:06:39.207Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us look at some of these numbers more carefully. FARM_F gave ~891932 which seems huge? Also FARM_T is ~888897063 which is astronomically large.\n# Also look at the units and energy vs power interpretation again.\n# For energy readings, we summed the values after conversion. But let us look at FARM_A: energy, kWh - 30-min intervals of readings? If each reading is energy accumulated over interval, summing them gives total. Or if each is instantaneous power/energy rate? But with 30-min intervals and values in kWh, sometimes they are meter readings (cumulative). Summing cumulative meter readings is wrong - we need the difference (last - first). That could explain very large totals for some farms.\n# Also check FARM_T: calibration says reading_type is energy, unit is MWh for FARM_T? Let us look up FARM_T in calibration.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
