timestamp=2026-11-09T12:07:06.856Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# FARM_T: energy, MWh. If the values are cumulative (total meter reading), summing all readings gives wrong total. We need total energy produced during the reporting day = final reading at end of day (or near end) minus initial reading at start of day (or before). Or if readings are interval energy (e.g., MWh in that interval), then sum is correct. Let us look at the actual values.\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/tmp')\nfrom loader2 import load_production\n\ndf = load_production('FARM_T')\n# filter to reporting day\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\nday_start = datetime(2024, 3, 15, 0, 0, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('UTC'))\nday_end = datetime(2024, 3, 16, 0, 0, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('UTC'))\nif df['timestamp'].dt.tz is None:\n    df['timestamp'] = df['timestamp'].dt.tz_localize('UTC')\nelse:\n    df['timestamp'] = df['timestamp'].dt.tz_convert('UTC')\ndfd = df[(df['timestamp']>=day_start)&(df['timestamp']<day_end)]\nprint(len(dfd))\nprint(dfd['mwh_yield'].head(5), '...', dfd['mwh_yield'].tail(5))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-11-09T12:07:06.856Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="tail -40" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
