timestamp=2026-11-09T12:10:23.878Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# There are odd values like -999 and 888888.8. Also the task says \"Any value that is negative must be dropped, this rule is valid only after the calibration offset is applied.\" So we do drop negatives after calibration - that removes -999. 888888.8 is a huge positive spike - but after calibration and considering it's a single reading? Or maybe it’s an error/outlier? But the task doesn’t explicitly say drop outliers, only negatives after calibration and duplicates handling, maintenance windows, etc.\n# But also look at the scale: FARM_A has installed capacity 800 kW. So values like 330 kW are reasonable power readings. If it's power (kW), then energy over 30 min interval is power * 0.5h. Summing those gives total kWh for the day - which sounds right. Let us look up FARM_A's sensor_info again.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
