timestamp=2026-11-09T12:15:04.055Z level=INFO run=1ef60999 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# FARM_F has readings every 15 min, so ~96 intervals per day total. After removing 8 intervals (11:00-13:00, 2 hours = 8 intervals of 15 min), ~88 intervals remain. And we have 69 after drop_duplicates? Let us count: we dropped duplicates - maybe many duplicates. Also in the data, the same timestamp might appear multiple times? Or duplicates based on full row? But regardless, the sum of interval energy values across the valid intervals in the day gives total production for the day. That is correct. For example, if each 15-min interval contributed ~13 kWh on average, total ~1100 kWh/day for a 700 kW plant - seems low. Or if each contributed ~100 kWh, total ~8800 kWh/day - also plausible.\n# But 891932 kWh total from a 700 kW plant is ~1274 capacity factor - impossible for a single day. That means either the unit is not kWh as stated, or we’re interpreting the values wrong. Let us look at what the actual values mean in context of other farms. Compare FARM_A (800 kW, got 3936 kWh total) vs FARM_F (700 kW, got 891932 kWh total) - completely different scale. That’s suspicious.\n# Let us look at the raw interval energy values for FARM_F before any filtering - what’s the magnitude?\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
